{"availability":"available","full":"Aadithyaar22/UrbanBites","name":"UrbanBites","description":"A multi-sided food delivery platform — a Swiggy/Zomato-style clone with a real consumer ordering flow, restaurant partner dashboard, delivery queue, and live analytics.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-31T14:59:10Z","updated":"2026-08-02T17:53:15Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://urbanbites-platform.netlify.app","topics":["food-delivery","fullstack","netlify","nextjs","postgresql","prisma","react","shadcn-ui","tailwindcss","typescript"],"demo":"https://urbanbites-platform.netlify.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:49.039Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:49.039Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:49.039Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T06:28:49.039Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A multi-sided cloud-kitchen delivery platform — built as a real, working product, not a mockup. Consumer ordering, a restaurant partner dashboard, a delivery queue, and live analytics, all backed by an actual Postgres database on an actual URL.","UrbanBites is a fictional cloud-kitchen brand that cooks six virtual restaurants — biryani, pizza, Chinese, burgers, desserts, and healthy bowls — out of one shared kitchen network. This repo is the full platform behind that brand: the app customers order from, the dashboard the kitchen runs on, the app delivery riders use, and the analytics the business is run by.","It was built to answer a specific brief: \"build a Swiggy/Zomato-style clone, production level, deploy it live with a hosted database, for free.\" Every box in that brief is actually checked — there's a real signup/login, a real order that moves through a real kitchen and a real delivery rider, and a real Postgres database you can query. Nothing here is localStorage pretending to be a backend."],"features":["Discovery feed — all 6 UrbanBites virtual restaurants, filterable by category,","searchable by name or cuisine.","Menu + cart — adding an item from a different restaurant than what's already in","your cart triggers a real confirmation dialog (\"start a new order?\"), matching how Swiggy/Zomato actually behave — not glossed over.","Checkout — pick a saved address or add a new one; pay through the mock gateway"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aadithyaar22/UrbanBites/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4fa504cbaa777d2f4b678f3a75bf479a9af0eb2c99972ffbe2b6e45b681fc895","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:49.184Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:49.184Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A multi-sided cloud-kitchen delivery platform — built as a real, working product, not a mockup. Consumer ordering, a restaurant partner dashboard, a delivery queue, and live analytics, all backed by an actual Postgres database on an actual URL.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aadithyaar22/UrbanBites/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"It was built to answer a specific brief: \"build a Swiggy/Zomato-style clone, production level, deploy it live with a hosted database, for free.\" Every box in that brief is actually checked — there's a real signup/login, a real order that moves through a real kitchen and a real delivery rider, and a real Postgres database you can query.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aadithyaar22/UrbanBites/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"timestamps, not a map embed (which needs its own paid API key).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aadithyaar22/UrbanBites/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"timestamps, not a map embed (which needs its own paid API key).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aadithyaar22/UrbanBites/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"4fa504cbaa777d2f4b678f3a75bf479a9af0eb2c99972ffbe2b6e45b681fc895","sourceUrl